        "collection_label": "The 12th Month",
        "index_url": "/pages/the-worktable",
        "title": "The Wrapping Paper",
        "subtitle": "Three prints, one little hour",
        "story": "<p>Flat sheets, not a roll: a roll never lies flat again, and this is meant to be kept. Uncoated, so it creases sharply and takes a pen. The reverse left plain, so once the gift is out of it the paper can be written on and posted.</p><p>For the one who wraps it properly on the kitchen table; not for someone in a hurry.</p>",
        "worktable_note": "Sheets or a roll. And whether December gets a print of its own, or the house mark is enough.",
